478
00:26:08,733 --> 00:26:10,401
<i>He'll love it.</i>

479
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:16,074
Sixth, sing "Happy Birthday" to him
on his birthday.

480
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:19,077
No one's ever done that for him.

481
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:30,588
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

482
00:26:31,756 --> 00:26:33,507
Tongtong, you're so sweet.

483
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:35,218
I'm so happy today.

484
00:26:37,137 --> 00:26:39,305
<i>It's Strawberry Candy's birthday today.</i>

485
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:41,640
<i>Let's wish him a happy birthday!</i>

486
00:26:41,641 --> 00:26:43,434
<i>Everybody sing. Ready, go!</i>

487
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:58,491
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

488
00:26:59,492 --> 00:27:00,869
<i>Blow out the candles.</i>

489
00:27:02,495 --> 00:27:03,330
<i>Happy birthday!</i>

490
00:27:10,879 --> 00:27:11,755
Ruyi.

491
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:14,048
No way!

492
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:16,842
He's awake!

493
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:19,637
This is amazing! Hurry...

494
00:27:21,806 --> 00:27:24,267
Oppa, don't go.

495
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:27,186
Please don't go.

496
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:31,816
Unnie, do you remember everything he said?

497
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,653
First,

498
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:38,740
- don't ask me to be too gentle.
- Quiet!

499
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:44,954
Second, don't let me have
more than three drinks, or I'll...

500
00:27:46,206 --> 00:27:47,665
I'm not that thirsty yet.

501
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:49,959
I missed

502
00:27:50,543 --> 00:27:51,920
all that part.

503
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:55,339
Taozi, you finally have your own crib!

504
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,965
- That should do it.
- It's so cute.

505
00:27:56,966 --> 00:27:58,675
- All set.
- How much? I'll pay you.

506
00:27:58,676 --> 00:28:00,303
No, it's okay.

507
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:04,181
No. My livestream made money.
I sold out, so I can afford it.

508
00:28:04,182 --> 00:28:07,602
Aren't you saving for a nanny?
This is my gift to Taozi.

509
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,270
Taozi, wanna try it out?

510
00:28:10,271 --> 00:28:11,606
Let's try it out.

511
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:13,440
Careful.

512
00:28:13,441 --> 00:28:15,443
It's your crib!

513
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,239
Comfy?

514
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:24,536
She's smiling! So happy!

515
00:28:25,995 --> 00:28:28,415
Mommy's so happy.

516
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:35,088
When I first became a mom, it was so hard.

517
00:28:36,256 --> 00:28:37,632
I worked so hard every day.

518
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:41,302
But seeing her smile
makes it all worth it.

519
00:28:41,886 --> 00:28:43,805
I was waiting for your smile, huh?

520
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,059
You don't have to be strong. I'm here.

521
00:28:49,644 --> 00:28:50,770
What do you mean?

522
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:53,939
No, nothing.

523
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:58,360
I mean, you've got me to help you now,
so you can... yeah.

524
00:28:58,361 --> 00:29:02,073
So, who did you buy
all that intimate wash for?

525
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:06,368
You said it works really well.
Who cares who it's for?

526
00:29:06,369 --> 00:29:07,661
That many female friends?

527
00:29:07,662 --> 00:29:08,912
No, they're all guys.

528
00:29:08,913 --> 00:29:11,207
Yeah, just some guy friends.

529
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:15,462
You like it?

530
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:18,714
I heard they can only see
within 20 centimeters.

531
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,133
That close?

532
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:25,262
Why did you come back?

533
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:26,889
You love her that much?

534
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:28,599
A-li loves her, too.

535
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,144
And people should be with people, okay?

536
00:29:54,417 --> 00:29:56,503
- Why are you smiling?
- Ruyi and I...

537
00:29:57,378 --> 00:29:58,630
You scared me to death!

538
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:01,965
No guilty conscience, no fear of ghosts.

539
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:03,802
Says the ghost.

540
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:07,054
You and Ruyi seem pretty close lately.

541
00:30:07,055 --> 00:30:08,973
Laughing and chatting over dinner.

542
00:30:10,141 --> 00:30:13,101
That's how normal people eat together.

543
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:17,189
You're always at home
so you wouldn't get it.

544
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:19,192
So you two are always like this now?

545
00:30:19,859 --> 00:30:21,027
Like what?

546
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:30,245
What? Why the big sigh?

547
00:30:32,121 --> 00:30:33,540
What's wrong? Are you upset?

548
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:38,293
Yeah. I should be happy,
but I'm also kind of upset.

549
00:30:38,294 --> 00:30:39,838
I don't know why.

550
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:44,592
Let me ask you something.

551
00:30:45,385 --> 00:30:47,135
Before...

552
00:30:47,136 --> 00:30:48,387
Before you died,

553
00:30:48,388 --> 00:30:50,890
were you secretly in love with Chang Ruyi?

554
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:53,350
Ruyi told you?

555
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:57,646
No, I just guessed.
I mean, you were so good to her.

556
00:30:57,647 --> 00:30:59,815
You liked her, right?

557
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:02,318
You're good to her. You like her, too?

558
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:08,366
No, I don't.

559
00:31:08,992 --> 00:31:10,033
I...

560
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:13,913
I'm only nice to her
because you told me to be.

561
00:31:14,497 --> 00:31:15,455
Right?

562
00:31:15,456 --> 00:31:16,915
I'm a gangster.

563
00:31:16,916 --> 00:31:20,168
I could die anytime, just like you.

564
00:31:20,169 --> 00:31:22,422
I don't show my feelings that easily.

565
00:31:26,801 --> 00:31:28,511
Anyway, that's not the point.

566
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:31,680
Have you been looking for Grandma?

567
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:34,016
Checked Northeast Coast and Kenting.

568
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,768
- No ghosts--
- Kenting?

569
00:31:37,186 --> 00:31:40,439
Kenting is Kenting,
and Hengchun is Hengchun.

570
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:43,150
Just like Taoyuan is Taoyuan
and Zhongli is Zhongli.

571
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:44,610
You weren't even looking!

572
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:47,113
No ghost has seen your grandma.

573
00:31:48,072 --> 00:31:50,199
Maybe she's been reincarnated.

574
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:53,828
Maybe Grandma won't see me.

575
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:57,165
Can you...

576
00:31:58,207 --> 00:32:00,960
check if she's been reincarnated?

577
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:27,277
Let me ask you.

578
00:32:27,278 --> 00:32:29,821
To know if someone's reincarnated,

579
00:32:29,822 --> 00:32:32,199
do you have to ask
the Black and White Reaper?

580
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:35,828
Yeah, but he'll probably take you away
the moment you show up.

581
00:32:37,246 --> 00:32:38,915
Who are you checking on?

582
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:42,502
A friend's grandma. We're not that close.

583
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:45,254
Then why help him?

584
00:32:46,130 --> 00:32:50,134
I asked him to look after her,
but now I don't want him to.

585
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:52,595
That's called jealousy.

586
00:32:53,304 --> 00:32:54,889
You're jealous of your friend.

587
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:57,641
Is that really bad of me?

588
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:59,393
That's totally normal.

589
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:00,644
I haven't reincarnated

590
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,897
because I want my boyfriend
to remember me.

591
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:07,235
Sometimes I visit his dreams
and remind him I'm still here.

592
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:10,113
But if he can't move on

593
00:33:10,863 --> 00:33:13,991
or find someone new, wouldn't that be sad?

594
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,535
What about me?

595
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:18,120
Love is selfish.

596
00:33:18,121 --> 00:33:20,999
Why else would you be
jealous of your friend?

597
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:23,084
You've got a point.

598
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:28,256
But I don't think she likes me back.

599
00:33:29,632 --> 00:33:31,217
Then go find out.

600
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:37,348
You said you can enter dreams.

601
00:34:40,536 --> 00:34:41,579
<i>You're back.</i>

602
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:46,249
Listen, I fed her, changed her diaper,
did squats and played "Poison,"

603
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,584
but she keeps crying.

604
00:34:47,585 --> 00:34:48,543
I don't know.

605
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:52,172
I read that white noise helps,
so I tried the hair dryer...

606
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:55,175
Look, Taozi's still crying.

607
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,427
It's okay...

608
00:34:58,346 --> 00:34:59,638
I heard taking her

609
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:01,765
for a drive might help. Wanna try?

610
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:03,308
- A drive?
- Can we?

611
00:35:03,309 --> 00:35:05,185
Okay, I'll get the car.

612
00:35:05,186 --> 00:35:08,063
I parked farther away because it's free.

613
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:09,648
I'll call you when I'm back.

614
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:11,817
- Okay.
- Keep your ringer on.

615
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,237
Sleeping so soundly. Little brat.

616
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:16,572
Do you really...

617
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:19,283
not know who

618
00:35:20,034 --> 00:35:21,911
Taozi's father is?

619
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:25,039
I don't know.

620
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:29,584
It was a one-night stand at a nightclub.

621
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:33,589
No, I was just asking.
I didn't mean anything by it.

622
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:38,760
I just think you're amazing
for choosing to have her.

623
00:35:38,761 --> 00:35:41,347
That took a lot of courage.

624
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,016
Back then...

625
00:35:45,017 --> 00:35:47,436
I actually wasn't planning to have her.

626
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:49,564
But...

627
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:54,735
when I went to see the doctor later,
they told me her due date was April 1st,

628
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:57,238
my sister's birthday.

629
00:35:58,197 --> 00:35:59,615
You have a sister?

630
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:03,911
My sister was three years younger than me.

631
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:06,372
When she was three,

632
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:10,501
we took a nap together,

633
00:36:11,419 --> 00:36:13,254
and she never woke up.

634
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:18,384
I've always blamed myself
for not taking better care of her.

635
00:36:23,389 --> 00:36:24,765
So...

636
00:36:25,808 --> 00:36:29,519
that's why you got so mad
when I left Taozi and ran out?

637
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:31,814
Because of your sister?

638
00:36:33,107 --> 00:36:35,651
I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

639
00:36:37,486 --> 00:36:38,653
No, it's okay.

640
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:43,242
Now that I'm older, I tell myself
that I was only six. What did I know?

641
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:45,703
It wasn't my fault. I...

642
00:36:46,829 --> 00:36:49,081
I didn't know how to take care of a child.

643
00:36:51,584 --> 00:36:53,211
But when the doctor said

644
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:58,216
her due date was April 1st,
I felt like my sister had come back to me.

645
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:00,676
So...

646
00:37:01,636 --> 00:37:02,887
this time...

647
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,057
I wanted her to grow up well.

648
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:12,229
But I still keep messing up.

649
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:15,274
No, you're taking great care of her.

650
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:18,235
And what does being a "good parent"
even mean?

651
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:21,112
Tons of first-time parents
ask questions online.

652
00:37:21,113 --> 00:37:23,740
Some things you only learn as they happen.

653
00:37:23,741 --> 00:37:27,161
Everyone learns to be a parent
while raising their child.

654
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:32,832
And Taozi's adorable.

655
00:37:32,833 --> 00:37:34,167
This may sound weird,

656
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:40,299
but having her was
the best decision you ever made.

657
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:44,679
Though I don't know what your worst was.

658
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:50,643
I think she's really cute, too.

659
00:37:59,110 --> 00:38:00,194
Can you fold it up?

660
00:38:06,075 --> 00:38:07,159
Yeah.

661
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:11,205
Wow, that was pretty easy.

662
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:15,293
That smells delicious.

663
00:38:17,503 --> 00:38:19,130
Just take yours.

664
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:22,717
It's cold.

665
00:38:23,926 --> 00:38:25,010
Let's celebrate.

666
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:26,928
Taozi rarely sleeps this early.

667
00:38:26,929 --> 00:38:28,972
Just so you know, I'm a lightweight.

668
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:30,849
Beer's just water...

669
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:32,684
My grandma used to make...

670
00:38:32,685 --> 00:38:34,770
You're breastfeeding. Can you drink?

671
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:36,980
I'll just smell it.

672
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,399
Just smell it?

673
00:38:39,442 --> 00:38:40,775
The smell of freedom.

674
00:38:40,776 --> 00:38:42,527
That sounds rough.

675
00:38:42,528 --> 00:38:44,654
I'll have a little with you.

676
00:38:44,655 --> 00:38:45,948
Cheers!

677
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:52,954
This tastes awful!

678
00:38:52,955 --> 00:38:54,998
- You're sipping too little.
- No, I didn't know...

679
00:38:54,999 --> 00:38:56,082
What's so fun about this?

680
00:38:56,083 --> 00:38:58,461
Take big gulps, like this. Gulp, gulp!

681
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:01,546
Yeah?

682
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:03,215
See? Gulp...

683
00:39:08,721 --> 00:39:09,972
Wow, that was a big gulp!

684
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:12,850
Nice, huh?

685
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:17,145
It tastes awful!

686
00:39:17,146 --> 00:39:18,938
- No, it doesn't.
- This...

687
00:39:18,939 --> 00:39:20,358
This is so nice.

688
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:22,484
I'm really dizzy.

689
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:23,736
Is that normal?

690
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:27,823
This feels so good.

691
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:44,256
For real?

692
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:06,195
I blacked out.

693
00:40:13,369 --> 00:40:14,370
I feel like I've...

694
00:40:15,329 --> 00:40:16,539
seen this before.

695
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:18,666
I'm so sleepy.

696
00:40:42,898 --> 00:40:43,773
<i>Dreamwalking is easy.</i>

697
00:40:43,774 --> 00:40:48,362
Put your hand on their forehead
and silently say their name three times.

698
00:40:49,572 --> 00:40:51,449
Ruyi. Ruyi. Ruyi.

699
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:55,286
If she cares about you,
she'll cry when she sees you

700
00:40:55,870 --> 00:40:58,789
<i>in her dream.</i>

701
00:41:08,424 --> 00:41:09,550
Chang Ruyi.

702
00:41:10,342 --> 00:41:11,385
Chang Ruyi.

703
00:41:12,553 --> 00:41:13,804
Chang Ruyi.

704
00:41:38,829 --> 00:41:39,872
Strawberry Candy?

705
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:47,129
Ruyi.

706
00:41:48,756 --> 00:41:50,174
It's been a while.

707
00:42:03,229 --> 00:42:05,146
<i>I possessed someone once by accident.</i>

708
00:42:05,147 --> 00:42:09,276
How do I do it on purpose?

709
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:11,486
To possess someone,

710
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:15,573
just look them in the eyes
for three seconds.

711
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:16,700
That's all it takes?

712
00:42:17,409 --> 00:42:20,371
But ghosts shouldn't
possess people carelessly.

713
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:25,542
We could lose our souls.

714
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:27,670
Won't open.

715
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:36,637
You pinned me down.

716
00:42:38,138 --> 00:42:39,890
Did I say you could?

717
00:42:40,516 --> 00:42:41,725
I found your grandma.

718
00:42:42,518 --> 00:42:43,602
Where is she?

719
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:47,439
Look into my eyes. I'll take you to her.

720
00:42:48,148 --> 00:42:49,066
The underworld?

721
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:51,110
Kind of.

722
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:02,288
Wait...

723
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:04,622
Hurry! No time!

724
00:43:04,623 --> 00:43:06,584
Give me a second. I just woke up.

725
00:43:08,210 --> 00:43:10,211
Was that strong wind normal?

726
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:11,505
It's normal.

727
00:43:13,215 --> 00:43:14,340
Ready?

728
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:15,259
Here we go.

729
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:21,932
The wind's too strong.

730
00:43:38,407 --> 00:43:39,783
I'm sorry.

731
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:42,202
I need to borrow your body...

732
00:43:43,203 --> 00:43:44,955
so I can be with...

733
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:48,876
Ruyi.

734
00:43:51,837 --> 00:43:53,546
<i>Give me my body back, now!</i>

735
00:43:53,547 --> 00:43:58,259
I want to stay with you both forever.

736
00:43:58,260 --> 00:44:00,428
- Who was with me last night?
- Him.

737
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:02,263
Who cooks for me and takes care of Taozi?

738
00:44:02,264 --> 00:44:05,308
He asked me to do that, too.
You think I wanted to do it?

739
00:44:05,309 --> 00:44:07,645
You're not A-li. Who are you?

740
00:44:08,562 --> 00:44:09,480
Go to hell!

741
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:11,731
Die!

742
00:44:11,732 --> 00:44:13,191
- Shit!
- Damn!

743
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:16,111
<i>Why is this five million in your office?</i>
